\ Note: recover-quot has declared effect ( error -- ) so it must only consume the error

\ Success case - try-quot succeeds, recover-quot not called
[ 5 3 + ] [ drop ] recover
.

\ Error case - try-quot fails, recover-quot consumes error
[ drop ] [ drop ] recover
42 .

\ ignore-errors - error is suppressed
[ drop ] ignore-errors
"still running" .

\ ignore-errors with success - value left on stack
[ 100 ] ignore-errors
.

\ Nested recover - both recover quotations consume errors
[ [ drop ] [ drop ] recover ] [ drop ] recover
1 .
